====================================================================
  OVERALL FINDINGS TABLE
====================================================================
  saved table: Table_FINDINGS_overall_v9.csv
  - Inventory intensity (DIO) by sector: Varies ~4x: apparel/medical longest, mass-retail shortest.
      => Justifies peer-adjustment within super-group x year.
  - AbnInvPeer over time: Centred ~0 by construction; series noisy, no single clean COVID spike.
      => Use neutral framing; do not over-read the 2020-22 band.
  - AbnInvPeer vs next-yr ΔGM: Negative but modest: Pearson r=-0.075, OLS slope -0.0198.
      => Real but gentle descriptively; conditional regression is stronger.
  - Multicollinearity: Max VIF=1.01; AIG weakly correlated with controls.
      => AbnInvPeer is not proxying for size/leverage.
  - Distress decile gradient: Decile 1=15.7% -> decile 10=23.3%; trend +0.8pp/decile but NOT strictly monotonic.
      => Report as positively-trended, not monotonic (honest).
  - Geographic coverage: 279 firms, 14 countries; US is largest single domicile (59%).
      => Disclose: international extension of a US-anchored panel.
  - US vs international (Table 5): Near-identical medians (DIO 84 both); Mann-Whitney p=0.12.
      => US and non-US firms are descriptively comparable.
  - IFRS/GAAP comparability (Table 6): Same partition as US/non-US (every US firm=GAAP, every non-US=IFRS); DIO medians ~equal, p=0.12.
      => Accounting interpretation of the same split: LIFO-capability caveat does not distort DIO empirically.

